   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an application for\na real property tax exemption from Lubavitch of Old Westbury",
    "basePrintNo": "S5019",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5019-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5019\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an applica-\ntion for a real property tax exemption from Lubavitch of Old Westbury\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the County of Nassau to grant a real property tax exemption\nto Lubavitch of Old Westbury\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the County of Nassau to accept a retro-\nactive application for real property tax exemption for the property\nowned by Lubavitch of Old Westbury.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLubavitch of Old Westbury is a not-for-profit tax-exempt organization\nthat purchased property located in Nassau County at 153 Bacon Road, Old\nWestbury, New York 11568 for use as a synagogue (Nassau County tax map\nsection 19, block E, lot 2000). The transfer of ownership took place in\nMay of 2022 after the tax exempt filing deadline for the 21/22 and 22/23\ntax years. Although the exemption was granted, it was not granted\nretroactively to the date of purchase, therefore necessitating this\nlegislation. This legislation would provide Lubavitch of Old Westbury\nwith an exemption from real property taxes pursuant to 420-a of the Real\nProperty Tax Law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall effect immediately.\n",
