    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5019A\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an applica-\ntion for a real property tax exemption from Lubavitch of Old Westbury\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the County of Nassau to grant a real property tax exemption\nto Lubavitch of Old Westbury\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the County of Nassau to accept a retro\nactive application for real property tax exemption for the property\nowned by Lubavitch of Old Westbury.  Section 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLubavitch of Old. Westbury is a not-for-profit tax-exempt organization\nthat purchased property located in Nassau County at 153 Bacon Road, Old\nWestbury,\n  New  York  11568 for use as a synagogue (Nassau County tax map section\n19, block E, lot 2000). The transfer of ownership took place in  May  of\n2022  after  the  tax exempt filing deadline for the 21/22 and 22/23 tax\nyears. Although the exemption was granted, it was not  granted  retroac-\ntively  to  the  date  of  purchase, therefore necessitating this legis-\nlation. This legislation would provide Lubavitch of Old Westbury with an\nexemption from real property taxes pursuant to 462 of the Real  Property\nTax Law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall effect immediately.\n",
